!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/scoped-claim.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/35/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/35/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  The foreign side of a scope push ([TSON-SCHEMA] §7.8): a schema a subject's value names for itself
  with a nested `!!schema`, declaring a type the governing schema knows nothing about. Its identity is
  written into the subject directly rather than spliced, the corpus's own identities carrying no spec
  revision -- only the three bundled names do, which is the whole reason the splice exists.
  """
{
  claim => {
    id:     text
    amount: int32
  }

  @doc:"A second type in the same schema, so a vector can name one that is not the one admitted."
  remark => {
    text: text
  }
}
